  "question": {
    "text": "Number of spectral lines obtained in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>He</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math> spectra, when an electron makes transition from fifth excited state to first excited state will be"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula used here is:</p><p>Number of spectral lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></munderover><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>= Highest energy level=6(fifth excited state)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>=Lowest energy level=2(first excited state)</p><p>Number of spectral lines</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></munderover><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>Number of spectral lines in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>He</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math> for transition from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
